      "text": "The direction vector of the line is $\\vec{v} = \\langle 5-2, 1-2, -2-1 \\rangle = \\langle 3, -1, -3 \\rangle$. The parametric equations of the line can be written as:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx = 2 + 3t \\\\\ny = 2 - t \\\\\nz = 1 - 3t\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nwhere $t$ is a parameter. We are given that a point on the line has an $x$-coordinate of 4. We can substitute $x = 4$ into the first equation:\n\\[\n4 = 2 + 3t \\implies 3t = 2 \\implies t = \\frac{2}{3}\n\\]\nNow, we substitute $t = \\frac{2}{3}$ into the third equation to find the $z$-coordinate:\n\\[\nz = 1 - 3\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) = 1 - 2 = -1\n\\]\nThus, the $z$-coordinate of the point is $\\boxed{-1}$.",
